Ladybird gives a content script’s global a wrappedJSObject accessor
that returns the page realm’s global object, and nothing else about
the world changes. Gecko defines wrappedJSObject on every Xray wrapper,
in XrayWrapper.cpp’s wrappedJSObject_getter: it waives the Xray, so a
content script that reads window.wrappedJSObject gets the page’s own
window, expandos included. Blink and WebKit have no such affordance;
a Chrome extension that needs the page’s globals runs a script in
the MAIN world instead, and uBO’s Chromium build does exactly that.
